%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 02ff5e751dcfd764781b6d35bf16d1e0, type: 3}
  m_Name: Set_3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  setName: The Two Thrones
  narrativeSet:
  - paragraph: The king stands tall in the council hall. Envoys from the east speak
      in riddles, their smiles sharper than swords. Their time, shorter than they
      know.
    addEcon: 0
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: 0
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: "A sealed letter arrives at dawn \u2014 a treaty offer, or perhaps
      a trap. The wax bears a rival crest. The timing of which, could not be worse"
    addEcon: 0
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: 0
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: "Border fires burn through the night. Farmers flee, and the king\u2019s
      patience thins with every spark. The enemy appears to cave in from all sides.
      It's not just the monsters one must fear"
    addEcon: 1
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: -300
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: "In the great hall, the king\u2019s advisor whispers of spies within
      the court. Trust grows scarce as winter."
    addEcon: 0
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: -300
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: Gold flows from the treasury to bribe peace, yet greed knows no end.
      The neighboring duke demands more.
    addEcon: 1
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: -200
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: A banquet is held in fragile truce. Beneath silken words, daggers
      wait for their moment. But their are greater enemies on the border, monsters
      that do not sleep. Grin and bear.
    addEcon: 1
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: -50
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: "The rival kingdom marches soldiers along the border \u201Cfor training.\u201D
      The king knows better than to believe such lies."
    addEcon: 0
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: 0
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: An emissary brings gifts of silver and venom. The king accepts both
      with the same steady hand.
    addEcon: 1
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: 200
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: The King bides his time and sends scouts to attack a camp at night.
      Hiding under the guise of rogue theives, they bring back an abundance of gold.
    addEcon: 1
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: 400
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: Rumors spread that the rival queen has fallen ill. The king wonders
      if fate or poison struck first.
    addEcon: 0
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: 0
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: The royal banners, tattered but unfallen, flutter proudly in the smoke.
      The kingdom still breathes.
    addEcon: 0
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 0
    econ: 0
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 0
  - paragraph: Skeleton archers take position among the ruins. Their arrows sing
      the songs of death, but the living will answer.
    addEcon: 0
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 1
    econ: 0
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: -100
  - paragraph: The mines strike rich and gold floods the kingdom. Repairs take place.
      Monsters and Rivals stir
    addEcon: 1
    addInfrastructure: 0
    addTowerHealth: 1
    econ: 200
    infrastructure: {fileID: 0}
    towerHealth: 150
